---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { formatPounds } from '../lib/credits/money';
import { DEFAULT_SESSION_PRICE_PENCE } from '../lib/credits/ledger';

// The terms a household contact accepts before using the members' area. The
// training credit section describes the ledger as built: one balance per
// household, a session charged when a runner is signed in, corrections made
// as new entries. The decisions it rests on are listed for the committee in
// roadmap/committee/privacy-and-terms.md.

const sessionPrice = formatPounds(DEFAULT_SESSION_PRICE_PENCE);
const contact = 'info@omaghharriers.com';
---

<Layout title="Terms & Conditions — Omagh Harriers AC">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Terms and conditions</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">Last updated: November 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
      <p>
        These terms cover the Omagh Harriers AC members' area and training credit. You accept them
        when you first sign in. They sit alongside your membership of the club and the club's
        constitution and policies, and they don't replace any of them. Our
        <a href="/privacy" class="underline hover:text-gray-900">privacy notice</a> explains how we
        handle your information.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Your account</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          The members' area is for the contact of each member household. Your household is set up from
          your Klubfunder membership, and you sign in with the email address the club has for it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your account is personal. Don't share your sign-in link or let anyone else use your account.
          If you use a shared computer, sign out when you've finished.
        </li>
        <li>
          If your membership lapses, your access to the members' area stops. It comes back if you
          rejoin.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Training credit</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          Each household has one training credit balance, which any member of the household can use.
        </li>
        <li>
          When a registrar signs a member in at a session, the session's price is taken from the
          balance. A session currently costs {sessionPrice}. The price of a session is fixed when the
          session is set up, and a change in price never affects sessions that have already run.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can add credit by paying cash to a registrar at training or to a club administrator.
          Each payment appears on your statement with the date and the name of whoever recorded it.
        </li>
        <li>
          A balance can go below zero if a member trains without enough credit. Please top up at the
          next session you attend.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you'd like credit back as cash, ask a registrar at training or a club administrator. Only
          an administrator can move credit to another household. If you leave the club with credit
          remaining, contact us and we'll return it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Please check your statement. If something is wrong, tell a registrar or email us. Mistakes
          are corrected with a new entry rather than by changing the old one, so your statement always
          shows what happened and how it was put right.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Using the members' area</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          Use it only to manage your own household's membership and training credit.
        </li>
        <li>
          Don't try to see another household's information, or get round how the members' area works.
        </li>
        <li>
          We aim to keep the members' area available but can't promise it always will be. If it isn't
          working at a session, the registrar will use a paper sheet and record everything once it's
          back.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">If you volunteer as a registrar or administrator</h2>
      <p>The club trusts you with other families' information. In return:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          use it only to run training sessions or the club, and don't share, copy or screenshot it for
          anything else
        </li>
        <li>keep the phone or computer you use locked, and sign out of shared devices</li>
        <li>record payments when you take them, and never use another volunteer's account</li>
        <li>
          keep printed sign-in sheets and downloaded reports secure, and destroy them once what's on
          them has been recorded or is no longer needed
        </li>
        <li>
          tell the committee straight away if a phone or computer with club information on it is lost
          or stolen
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The club may withdraw registrar or administrator access at any time.</p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. We'll change the date at the top, and if a change affects your
        training credit or what you've agreed to, we'll tell household contacts by email or in the
        members' area before it takes effect.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms, your account or your training credit go to
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="underline hover:text-gray-900">{contact}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>These terms are governed by the law of Northern Ireland.</p>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 italic">
        Draft for the club committee's approval.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
